:: Arcology Skyline Avenue
<<location "arcology_skyline">><<run setup.arcology.visit("skyline")>><<effects>>
<<arcologyDangerCheck "skyline">><<if _arcologyDangerActive>><<exit>><</if>>
You are on Skyline Avenue, surrounded by apartment buildings. Some are so tall that their upper floors nearly reach the dome above the city. Every balcony has its own small garden, with trees, flowers, and grass.
<br><br>
<<arcologyStreetHazards>>
<<if !_arcologyHalt>>
	Places of interest
	<br>
	<<arcologyicon "residence">><<link [[Skyline Residences (0:02)|Arcology Skyline Residences]]>><<pass 2>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<arcologyicon "garden">><<link [[Sky terrace (0:05)|Arcology Sky Terrace]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
	<br><br>
	<<arcologyStreets "skyline">>
<</if>>

:: Arcology Skyline Residences
<<location "arcology_residences">><<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
The lobby of Skyline Residences is decorated with marble and real wood. Near the entrance, a receptionist stands behind a large, curved desk. At the other end of the room, a lift is waiting with its doors open.
<br><br>
Behind the desk, a large screen shows the different floors of the building, with names listed beside each one. You notice that the higher floors have fewer names, with only a handful of people listed near the top.
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Arcology Skyline Avenue]]>><<pass 2>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Sky Terrace
<<location "arcology_terrace">><<effects>>
The sky terrace is a public garden high above the city, built on a large platform connecting two towers. You walk towards the railing, where you can look down at most of the island.
<br><br>
<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
	At night, the city is full of lights from buildings, streets, and advertisements. Looking up, you can also see some of those lights reflected on the inside of the transparent dome covering the island.
<<else>>
	Nearby, a gardener is busy cutting the hedges. A small drone flies around the plants, occasionally getting close to where the gardener is working. When it comes too close, the gardener waves it away before continuing with the hedges.
<</if>>
<br><br>
A few benches are placed among the trees and flowers, away from the main path where people walk through the garden.
<br><br>
<<if setup.arcology.reliefLeft("terrace")>>
	<<arcologyicon "terrace">><<link [[Sit in the garden (0:30)|Arcology Sky Terrace]]>><<pass 30>><<run setup.arcology.relief("terrace")>><<stress -4>><<trauma -1>><</link>><<lstress>><<ltrauma>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Arcology Skyline Avenue]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Crown Avenue
<<location "arcology_crown">><<effects>>
<<if !setup.arcology.eliteAccess()>>
	As you approach the checkpoint at the end of Skyline Avenue, red warning lights turn on above the road. Two guards wearing white armour step in front of you, blocking the entrance to Crown Avenue.
	<br><br>
	<<holo "CROWN AVENUE / CHECKPOINT" "denied">>
		<<holoRow "VISITOR" `$xchange.arcology.handle or "UNREGISTERED"`>>
		<<holoRow "INVITED BY" "NO RESIDENT">>
		<<holoLine "ACCESS DENIED" "denied">>
	<</holo>>
	<br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Go back (0:10)|Arcology Skyline Avenue]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<exit>>
<</if>>
<<set _crownArrival to $xchange.arcology.district isnot "crown">>
<<run setup.arcology.visit("crown")>>
<<if _crownArrival>>
	As you reach the checkpoint, a scanner checks your implant.
	<br><br>
	It confirms that your sponsor has given you permission to enter Crown Avenue, so the guards let you walk past without asking any questions.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Crown Avenue]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<exit>>
<</if>>
<<arcologyDangerCheck "crown">><<if _arcologyDangerActive>><<exit>><</if>>
You are now on Crown Avenue, one of the most private and expensive areas of the city.
<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
	<br><br>
	Several expensive cars drive slowly past you without using their headlights. Their windows are so dark that you can't see the people inside, even when a car passes right beside you.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<arcologyStreetHazards>>
<<if !_arcologyHalt>>
	Places of interest
	<br>
	<<arcologyicon "compound">><<link [[The compounds (0:05)|Arcology Crown Compounds]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
	<br><br>
	<<arcologyStreets "crown">>
<</if>>

:: Arcology Crown Compounds
<<location "arcology_crown">><<effects>>
You walk along a road in one of the higher parts of the city, where large houses stand behind tall walls on both sides. These houses belong to wealthy families and powerful organisations, each controlling a different part of the island.
<br><br>
Every house has a black metal gate with a different symbol on it instead of a name. Guards stand near the entrances, watching people who walk past and making sure nobody enters without permission.
<br><br>
As you continue along the road, you can see parts of the gardens through some of the gates. However, the walls are so high that most of the houses remain hidden from the street, leaving you with little idea of what happens inside.
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Arcology Crown Avenue]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stillwater Court
<<location "arcology_stillwater">><<effects>>
<<arcologyVictorPronouns>>
<<set _stillwaterArrival to $xchange.arcology.district isnot "stillwater">>
<<run setup.arcology.visit("stillwater")>>
<<if _stillwaterArrival>>
	Near the end of Crown Avenue, you notice a large property surrounded by high walls. Unlike the other properties nearby, there are no decorations or signs on its walls, and you can't see what's inside.
	<br><br>
	Guards stand at the corners of the property, watching the street. None of them approach you as you walk towards the entrance.
	<br><br>
	Before you reach the gate, it opens. A tall <<print _vman>> wearing a neat dark coat steps outside to meet you. <<print _vHe>> seems to recognise you and gives you a small nod.
	"You've reached the end of Crown Avenue. My master isn't seeing visitors at the moment, but you're welcome to spend some time in the courtyard."
	<br><br>
	<<print _vHe>> moves aside, allowing you to enter through the gate.
	<br><br>
	Inside, you can see a large pool of water with a narrow stone path leading towards a white door. The <<print _vman>> follows you through the gate before walking ahead towards the door, leaving you free to look around.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Arcology Stillwater Court]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<exit>>
<</if>>
You are inside Stillwater Court, a quiet courtyard surrounded by high walls. A large, shallow pool takes up most of the space, with a narrow stone path crossing the water.
<br><br>
The water is so still that you can see the sky and the city's dome reflected in it.
<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
	Small lights beneath the water light up the stone path, allowing you to see where you're walking. The rest of the courtyard is dark.
<</if>>
<br>
<<arcologyStreetHazards>>
<<if !_arcologyHalt>>
	<<if setup.arcology.reliefLeft("stillwater")>>
		<<relaxicon>><<link [[Sit by the water (0:30)|Arcology Stillwater Court]]>><<pass 30>><<run setup.arcology.relief("stillwater")>><<stress -6>><</link>><<lstress>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<br>
	<<arcologyStreets "stillwater">>
<</if>>
